  "title": "Philadelphia Yellow Fever Epidemic of 1793",
  "summary": "Between August and November 1793 yellow fever struck Philadelphia, then the temporary U.S. capital. Sources estimate over 5,000 deaths among about 50,000 inhabitants. Thousands fled, most federal officials including Washington left, and commerce and city government were crippled. The government returned in November as deaths fell.",
